<https://kos.geospecimens.org/glossary/geological-collections-glossary>
    a                        skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:identifier       "geological-collections-glossary" ;
    skos:prefLabel           "Geological Collections Glossary"@en ;
    dcterms:title            "Geological Collections Glossary"@en ;
    skos:definition          """Terms and definitions supporting the Geological Collections Conceptual Data Model (GCDM), an ontologically grounded conceptual data model for geologic specimen collections. Terms are drawn from the Terms subsections of the GCDM manuscript and cover data modeling and ontology, compound specimens, names and classification systems, stratigraphy, geologic age, and geologic settings and sampling events."""@en ;
    dcterms:description      """Terms and definitions supporting the Geological Collections Conceptual Data Model (GCDM), an ontologically grounded conceptual data model for geologic specimen collections. Terms are drawn from the Terms subsections of the GCDM manuscript and cover data modeling and ontology, compound specimens, names and classification systems, stratigraphy, geologic age, and geologic settings and sampling events."""@en ;
    dcterms:creator          "Ben Norton" ;
    dcterms:publisher        "Ben Norton" ;
    dcterms:created          "2026-07-30"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified         "2026-07-30"^^xsd:date ;
    dcat:version             "2026-07-30" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri <https://kos.geospecimens.org/glossary/geological-collections-glossary/> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "gcdm" ;
    skos:scopeNote           "Covers the concepts required to interpret and implement the GCDM: data-modeling and ontology vocabulary, the compound specimen construct and its parts, names and classification systems, stratigraphic units, geologic age (relative and chronometric), and geologic settings and sampling events. Definitions are either reproduced from the cited standard or reference work, adapted from it, or authored for the GCDM; the provenance of each definition is recorded per term. Domain-specific classification values (e.g., individual Dana or Nickel-Strunz classes) are out of scope and are maintained in the GCDM Master Dictionary."@en ;
    skos:historyNote         "This glossary was created as part of the GeoSpecify and SwissCollNet programs. The terms and definitions are intended to accompany an upcoming publication Geological Collections Conceptual Data Model (GCDM)"@en ;
    skos:changeNote          "2026-07-30: Initial release. 105 terms extracted from the Terms subsections (§2.1, §3.1, §4.1, §5.1, §6.1, §7.1) of GCDM manuscript version 2026-07-27, with 44 cited sources resolved against the manuscript bibliography."@en ;
    dcterms:license          <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights           "Definitions reproduced or adapted from third-party standards and reference works remain the property of their respective rights holders and are cited in glossary-sources.csv. Compiled glossary (c) 2026 the GCDM authors, released under CC BY 4.0." ;
